# KB-Desk web viewer configuration
# Word-split into arguments for kbdesk-web.
#
# TLS is mandatory (HTTPS/WSS). The files below come from the
# launcher-generated set in /etc/kbdesk/tls (create once with:
#   cd /etc/kbdesk && sudo kbdesk relay --tls-dir tls   # Ctrl-C after start
# ), Let's Encrypt, or your corporate PKI. --tls-ca lets the bridge verify
# the relay when it uses a private CA; drop it when the relay presents a
# publicly trusted certificate. See docs/encryption-and-certificates.md.
#
# Visitors connect with only an ID + password (recommended):
#   KB_DESK_WEB_ARGS=--listen 0.0.0.0:8080 --relay relay.example.com:21118 --tls-cert /etc/kbdesk/tls/cert.pem --tls-key /etc/kbdesk/tls/key.pem --tls-ca /etc/kbdesk/tls/ca.pem
#
# Same-machine relay (typical `kbdesk serve`-in-systemd layout):
KB_DESK_WEB_ARGS=--listen 0.0.0.0:8080 --relay 127.0.0.1:21118 --tls-cert /etc/kbdesk/tls/cert.pem --tls-key /etc/kbdesk/tls/key.pem --tls-ca /etc/kbdesk/tls/ca.pem
